hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28020","Narrated Muhammad ibn Jafar, he said: narrated Shubah, from Habib, a man of the Ansar, from a freedwoman of theirs called Layla, narrating from my grandmother, she being Umm Umarah bint Kab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, so she brought food near to him, so he said to her: Eat. So she said: I am fasting. So he said: The angels bless the fasting person when food is eaten in his presence until they finish."
"28021","Narrated Waki, he said: narrated Shubah, from Habib ibn Zayd Al-Ansari, from a woman called Layla, from Umm Umarah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, so we brought food near to him, and some of those with him were fasting, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When food is eaten in the presence of the fasting person, the angels bless him."
